<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Level 1 -->

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Lash</defName>
    <label>lash</label>
    <description>Call a tentacle up from beneath the ground. It begins as a Sprout, earning growth through damage dealt and corpse meals. Graspers drag and constrict prey, Crushers cleave nearby hostiles, and Colossi mark the ground before a crushing slam. Mature tentacles still eat to mend wounds, replenish active shields and extend their stay.\n\nGold cultivation at the idol improves feeding, regeneration, special attacks and movement across every ordinary tentacle you summon.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Lash</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_SummonTentacle</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <range>19.9</range>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>1</level>
        <order>1</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.02</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>8</entropyGain>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_SummonPawn">
        <kind>Deepcaller_Tentacle</kind>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Grasp</defName>
    <label>grasp</label>
    <description>A tentacle erupts from the ground beneath the target and leashes it to that spot. The victim is slowed, and if it strays it is dragged back to the eruption point. This is a physical grip: mechs, golems and other non-organic enemies can be held even if they are psychically deaf or inedible.\n\nThe deep holds harder when well fed: an Idol's devotion extends the grip's duration and makes it harder to tear free. Damage from any source, including your own tentacles, can tear the victim free early.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Grasp</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Grasp</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>30</castTime>
    <range>19.9</range>
    <durationTime>900</durationTime>
    <targetMode>Pawn</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
      <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
      <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
      <canTargetEntities>true</canTargetEntities>
      <onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>false</onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>1</level>
        <order>2</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.05</psyfocusCost>
        <psychic>false</psychic>
        <entropyGain>12</entropyGain>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.AbilityExtension_Hediff">
        <hediff>Deepcaller_Grasped</hediff>
        <severity>1</severity>
        <targetOnlyEnemies>true</targetOnlyEnemies>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <!-- Level 2 -->

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Riptide</defName>
    <label>riptide</label>
    <description>The deep makes projectiles of everything loose in the area: enemies, allies, animals, vehicles, corpses and scattered possessions. The pull starts strongest at the outer edge, weakest near the center. At the exact center, it only turns you around. Objects accelerate inward and build momentum along their actual path. At the center, acceleration ends but speed remains: projectiles coast onward. Air and impacts only slow them after crossing. Before then, the god replenishes momentum losses while collisions consume HP; intact obstacles still block passage. Newly dropped loot stays outside that cast.\n\nCollisions hurt both objects. A heavy, fast projectile can excavate a mountain or smash your base; it takes recoil and may destroy itself. Slow impacts can glance off armor. Weight resists a weak current, but a well-fed god turns that mass into destructive force. Nothing is mined without a projectile hitting it. Unsupported roofs can collapse.\n\nThree independent gold favors: spare our walls, spare our people from being thrown, and spare our possessions from being thrown. Each requires its own purchase and a sated idol on this map. Spared creatures and possessions still take collision damage. Walls do not protect your baubles; people do not protect your walls. Unclaimed chunks remain dangerous projectiles.\n\nGold can increase acceleration. At 5,000 devotion, separate purchases extend the pull area and cast distance. Grasp is the precise hold. Riptide is calamity.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Riptide</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Riptide</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <!-- No cooldown: entropy (20) and psyfocus are the real limiters, and
         any cooldown at all outlives the ~1.3s drag, making the mid-drag
         redirect recast unreachable. (VEF cooldownTime is in TICKS; the
         VPE_PsycastBase default is 120 = 2s.) -->
    <cooldownTime>0</cooldownTime>
    <!-- The current flows under the ground, not over it: no line of sight
         needed, so you can surge behind walls and drag enemies into them. -->
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>30</castTime>
    <range>24.9</range>
    <radius>6.9</radius>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
      <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
      <canTargetEntities>true</canTargetEntities>
      <onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>false</onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>
      <canTargetBuildings>true</canTargetBuildings>
      <mapObjectTargetsMustBeAutoAttackable>false</mapObjectTargetsMustBeAutoAttackable>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>2</level>
        <order>2</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.15</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>20</entropyGain>
        <psychic>false</psychic>
        <!-- Riptide is unusable below 10 idol devotion, so it must sit
             behind Raise Idol in the tree — otherwise the point is a trap
             for anyone without an idol. NOTE: VPE prerequisites are OR
             (PrereqsCompleted uses Any), so exactly one entry here. -->
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_RaiseIdol</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_Riptide">
        <!-- Baseline pull: 5 ticks/cell, accelerated by devotion and resisted
             by actual mass. Vehicle Framework mass includes its cargo. -->
        <ticksPerCell>5</ticksPerCell>
        <stunTicks>120</stunTicks>
        <ringWidth>1.4</ringWidth>
        <!-- Devotion economy: casting requires minDevotion. Cast range gets
             +1 cell per 5 devotion (capped +8). AoE radius follows the
             curve below, then +2 cells per devotion doubling above 2160.
             Free radius is bounded at 32. Purchased radius and cast-distance
             extensions raise their limits independently, up to the map size. -->
        <minDevotion>10</minDevotion>
        <devotionPerBonusCell>5</devotionPerBonusCell>
        <maxBonusCells>8</maxBonusCells>
        <radiusByDevotion>
          <points>
            <li>(10, 2)</li>
            <li>(80, 8)</li>
            <li>(240, 12)</li>
            <li>(2160, 16)</li>
          </points>
        </radiusByDevotion>
        <!-- Base pressures: flesh/debris 3 + 0.4D; rock/structures D. Actual
             impact scales with run-up, mass and relative speed. No radial
             falloff or automatic area mining. Structure protection is a
             purchased favor that requires a sated local idol. -->
        <collisionDamageBase>3</collisionDamageBase>
        <collisionDamagePerDevotion>0.4</collisionDamagePerDevotion>
        <wallDamageBase>0</wallDamageBase>
        <wallDamagePerDevotion>1</wallDamagePerDevotion>
        <visualDurationTicks>120</visualDurationTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_RaiseIdol</defName>
    <label>raise idol</label>
    <description>Raise an Idol of the Deep from the crust. Corpses left within its shadow are drawn under as offerings, building devotion. A fed god deepens its gifts: its powers reach farther and the leviathan rises stronger. Every tentacle still begins as a sprout and earns its own growth through battle.\n\nIf an idol already stands, it sinks beneath the crust and rises anew at the target — devotion, hunger and hoard intact. There is only ever one god.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/RaiseIdol</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_RaiseIdol</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>300</castTime>
    <range>9.9</range>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>2</level>
        <order>1</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.5</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>30</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Lash</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <!-- Ability_SpawnBuilding reads AbilityExtension_Building (not
           AbilityExtension_Spawn, which belongs to Ability_Spawn) -->
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.AbilityExtension_Building">
        <building>Deepcaller_Idol</building>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_InkVeil</defName>
    <label>ink veil</label>
    <description>The deep exhales a rolling cloud of abyssal ink over the target area. Gunfire through the murk goes wild and turrets cannot find their mark. Ink coats hostile eyes and sensors alike: mechs, golems and psychically deaf enemies are not exempt. The veil disperses on the wind, as all things return to the deep.\n\nCast it over your tentacles and let them fight in the dark they were born to.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/InkVeil</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_InkVeil</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <!-- Like Riptide: the ink rises from below, no line of sight needed. -->
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>30</castTime>
    <range>24.9</range>
    <radius>4.9</radius>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
      <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
      <canTargetEntities>true</canTargetEntities>
      <onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>false</onlyTargetPsychicSensitive>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>2</level>
        <order>3</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.1</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>15</entropyGain>
        <psychic>false</psychic>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Lash</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_InkVeil">
        <!-- Cloud grows +1 radius per 5 devotion, capped +10. Hostiles in
             the bloom are Inked (Sight debuff): severity 0.25 + 0.01 per
             devotion — stages at 0.45 (Sight x0.4) and 0.75 (x0.15), decays
             at 8/day so deeper ink also lasts longer. -->
        <devotionPerBonusCell>5</devotionPerBonusCell>
        <maxBonusCells>10</maxBonusCells>
        <inkSeverityBase>0.25</inkSeverityBase>
        <inkSeverityPerDevotion>0.01</inkSeverityPerDevotion>
        <visualDurationTicks>900</visualDurationTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <!-- Level 3 -->

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Consume</defName>
    <label>consume</label>
    <description>The deep swallows living flesh whole. Instant death; no corpse — the flesh becomes devotion. Health, wealth and combat strength pass through the caster as neural heat. Early arrogance is fatal: exceed your remaining heat capacity and the deep eats you too.\n\nDevotion and purchased burn reduction make greater offerings survivable. Each purchased radius tile permanently widens Consume, swallowing nearby organic creatures regardless of allegiance and increasing the strain. The caster is excluded from the offering, but never from the consequences.\n\nOne powerful boss can turn an ordinary feast into a fatal cast. Wound your prey, judge its worth, and leave room for the unknown.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Consume</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Consume</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <range>19.9</range>
    <targetMode>Pawn</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetPawns>true</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
      <canTargetAnimals>true</canTargetAnimals>
      <canTargetMechs>false</canTargetMechs>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>3</level>
        <order>1</order>
        <!-- Worth-based heat is charged by Ability_Consume. -->
        <psyfocusCost>0.05</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>0</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_RaiseIdol</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_Consume">
        <heatPerHitPoint>0.4</heatPerHitPoint>
        <liveOfferingFactor>1.5</liveOfferingFactor>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Bud</defName>
    <label>bud</label>
    <description>Plant a rooted bud of the deep on the target square. It cannot move, but watches a pistol's distance around itself and spits ghost-fire at hostiles for twice as long as a Sprout normally remains.\n\nA fed idol on the map strengthens its bolts. Gold cultivation permanently improves every Bud across all maps: damage, fire rate and bolt speed, with piercing fire, paired volleys and spectral trails at rank milestones. Excess cadence and speed become stronger impacts.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Bud</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_SummonTentacle</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>60</castTime>
    <range>24.9</range>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>3</level>
        <order>2</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.08</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>12</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Lash</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_SummonPawn">
        <kind>Deepcaller_Bud</kind>
        <count>1</count>
        <exactCell>true</exactCell>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <!-- Level 4 -->

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_DeepHoard</defName>
    <label>Passive: Deep Hoard</label>
    <description>Passive Skill: Unlocking this ability will automatically apply its effect.\n\nThe deep learns to keep what it cannot digest. Equipment, apparel and belongings of creatures devoured by Consume survive into the idol's belly, and can be ransomed back — for silver laid within the idol's shadow, at the deep's own generous valuation of their worth.\n\nThe deep is a god, not a charity.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/DeepHoard</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Passive</abilityClass>
    <targetMode>Self</targetMode>
    <castTime>0</castTime>
    <range>0</range>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>4</level>
        <order>1</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>0</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Consume</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Overgrowth</defName>
    <label>overgrowth</label>
    <description>The caller screams into the ground, and the deep answers all at once: every tentacle on the map surges forward one full growth stage, wounds knitting and lost flesh regrowing as it swells.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Overgrowth</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Overgrowth</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>90</castTime>
    <targetMode>Self</targetMode>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>4</level>
        <order>2</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.25</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>30</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Lash</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Symbiote</defName>
    <label>symbiote</label>
    <description>Graft a living tentacle of the deep onto your own flesh. Once mastered, each graft lends dexterity scaled to the idol's devotion when it was taken — but a fresh graft is a shock the body must grow into over many days.\n\nThe deep permits the first graft freely. Each one after tempts it: fail its regard, and the tentacle devours its host.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Symbiote</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Symbiote</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <castTime>120</castTime>
    <targetMode>Self</targetMode>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>4</level>
        <order>3</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.2</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>25</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Consume</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_Symbiote">
        <!-- Max bonus = devotion/100 capped at +25 (1000 -> +10, 2500 ->
             +25); grafts start at -10 and adapt up. Fail chances by grafts
             already carried: the tentacle eats the caster. -->
        <devotionPerBonusPoint>100</devotionPerBonusPoint>
        <maxBonusPerGraft>25</maxBonusPerGraft>
        <startingBonus>-10</startingBonus>
        <failChances>
          <li>0</li>
          <li>0.05</li>
          <li>0.10</li>
          <li>0.20</li>
          <li>0.40</li>
          <li>0.80</li>
        </failChances>
        <liveOfferingFactor>1.5</liveOfferingFactor>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <!-- Level 5 -->

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_LeviathansWake</defName>
    <label>leviathan's wake</label>
    <description>Wake the deep itself. A vast head, eight hunting arms, and three stilling flowers breach through separate apertures into one submerged god. Every limb chooses prey within the body's reach while the head spits abyssal sludge that scales with the victim and leaves its defenses yielding.\n\nThe leviathan's flesh is one: wound any aperture and it is the whole that bleeds, one single enormous pool of vitality scaled by the idol's devotion. When the pool is spent — or the deep's patience — the whole god sinks at once.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/LeviathansWake</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_LeviathansWake</abilityClass>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>300</castTime>
    <range>29.9</range>
    <targetMode>Location</targetMode>
    <targetingParameters>
      <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
      <canTargetSelf>false</canTargetSelf>
      <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
      <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
    </targetingParameters>
    <castSound>VPE_Enthrall_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>5</level>
        <order>1</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0.85</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>60</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_Overgrowth</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
      <li Class="Deepcaller.AbilityExtension_Leviathan">
        <headKind>Deepcaller_LeviathanHead</headKind>
        <armKind>Deepcaller_LeviathanArm</armKind>
        <flowerKind>Deepcaller_LeviathanFlower</flowerKind>
        <armCount>8</armCount>
        <flowerCount>3</flowerCount>
        <ringRadius>3</ringRadius>
        <flowerRingRadius>2.15</flowerRingRadius>
        <!-- Shared pool: 1500 + 2/devotion -->
        <basePool>1500</basePool>
        <poolPerDevotion>2</poolPerDevotion>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef ParentName="VPE_PsycastBase">
    <defName>Deepcaller_Tideguard</defName>
    <label>Passive: Tideguard</label>
    <description>Passive Skill: Unlocking this ability will automatically apply its effect.\n\nTentacles you summon rise wrapped in a skin of pressurized deep-water force — an energy shield that scales with their growth stage, from a thin film on a sprout to beyond shield-belt strength on a colossus. Like all such shields it stops projectiles, not blades, and breaks under EMP.\n\nThe leviathan's head is the deep itself. It does not hide behind shields.</description>
    <iconPath>UI_Deepcaller/Abilities/Tideguard</iconPath>
    <abilityClass>Deepcaller.Ability_Passive</abilityClass>
    <targetMode>Self</targetMode>
    <castTime>0</castTime>
    <range>0</range>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.AbilityExtension_Psycast">
        <path>Deepcaller_Path</path>
        <level>5</level>
        <order>2</order>
        <psyfocusCost>0</psyfocusCost>
        <entropyGain>0</entropyGain>
        <prerequisites>
          <li>Deepcaller_LeviathansWake</li>
        </prerequisites>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>

</Defs>
